abstract:
We study the regularity properties of a weak solution to the boundary value problem for the equation $-\Delta ho +a u=f$ in a bounded domain $\Omega\subset \mathbb{R}^N$, where $ho=e^{-\mbox{div}\left(|
abla u|^{p-2}
abla u+ eta_0|
abla u|^{-1}
abla uight)}$. This problem is derived from the mathematical modeling of crystal surfaces. It is known that the exponent term can exhibit singularity. In this paper we obtain a partial regularity result for the weak solution. It asserts that there exists an open subset $\Omega_0\subset \Omega$ such that $|\Omega\setminus\Omega_0|=0$ and the exponent term is locally bounded in $\Omega_0$. Furthermore, if $x_0\in \Omega\setminus\Omega_0$, then $ho$ vanishes of $N+2-\varepsilon$ order at $x_0$ for each $\varepsilon\in(0,2)$. Our results reveal that the exponent term behaves well if it stays away from negative infinity.

$\mathfrak{L}_{II}$ operator is introduced by Y.-L. Xin (\emph{Calculus of Variations and Partial Differential Equations. 2015, 	extbf{54}(2):1995-2016)}, which is an important extrinsic elliptic differential operator of divergence type and has profound geometric meaning. In this paper, we extend $\mathfrak{L}_{II}$ operator to more general elliptic differential operator $\mathfrak{L}_{
u}$, and investigate the clamped plate problem of bi-$\mathfrak{L}_{
u}$ operator, which is denoted by $\mathfrak{L}_{
u}^{2}$, on the complete Riemannian manifolds. A general formula of eigenvalues for the $\mathfrak{L}_{
u}^{2}$ operator is established. Applying this formula, we estimate the eigenvalues with lower order on the Riemannian manifolds. As some further applications, we establish some eigenvalue inequalities for this operator on the translating solitons with respect to the mean curvature flows, submanifolds of the Euclidean spaces, unit spheres and projective spaces. In particular, for the case of translating solitons, all of the eigenvalue inequalities are universal.

We consider the moduli space $\mathcal{M}_{
u}$ of torsion-free, asymptotically conical (AC) Spin(7)-structures which are defined on the same manifold and asymptotic to the same Spin(7)-cone with decay rate $
u<0$. We show that $\mathcal{M}_{
u}$ is an orbifold if $
u$ is a generic rate in the non-$L^2$ regime $(-4,0)$. Infinitesimal deformations are given by topological data and solutions to a non-elliptic first-order PDE system on the compact link of the asymptotic cone. As an application, we show that the classical Bryant-Salamon metric on the bundle of positive spinors on $S^4$ has no continuous deformations as an AC Spin(7)-metric.

